    "name": "School API — Admin Session",
    "description": "Platform admin session. **Documented:** `GET|POST|DELETE /admin/session`.\n\n- `POST` requires `{{adminHost}}` (`admin.<rootHost>`).\n- `GET` requires Bearer `{{accessToken}}` (host **not** checked).\n- `DELETE` always `200 { ok: true }` (token optional; host not checked).\n- Test script on sign-in writes `{{accessToken}}`.\n\nShared environment: `environments/School-API.local.postman_environment.json`.\n\n- `{{baseUrl}}` is the **backend** (`http://127.0.0.1:5000`), not Next on `3000`.\n- Prefer `x-school-host` over `Host`. Matching lowercases and strips `:{port}`.\n- Tokens are HMAC (`payload.signature`), not JWT. Admin `{{accessToken}}` will not verify on school/campus routes (different HMAC material). School and campus share `:school-account-session`.\n- Error JSON (except health): `{ \"error\": \"<string>\" }`. No 422. Wrapper-only 500 is `{ \"error\": \"Internal server error\" }`.\n- Do not invent routes or status codes. Later batches land in the matching collection file — do not grow a monolith.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://127.0.0.1:5000"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Admin Session",
      "description": "Platform-operator session on `admin.<rootHost>` only. Identity is `platform.admins`, not a tenant.\n\nSign-in is the only method that enforces the admin host. GET validates the HMAC Bearer token and does **not** re-check host. DELETE always returns 200 and does not read the token.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Read platform admin session",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{accessToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
                "description": "HMAC session token from POST /admin/session. Missing, non-Bearer, expired, or bad signature → 401."
              },
              {
                "key": "x-school-host",
                "value": "{{adminHost}}",
                "description": "Sent by the Next console. **Not validated** on GET — only the Bearer token matters."
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/session",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "admin",
                "session"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Returns the current platform-admin identity if the Bearer token is valid.\n\n**Auth:** required. `Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}`. `readBearerToken` only accepts a header that starts with `Bearer `.\n\n**Who:** the signed-in platform operator. School directors, campus users, and guests cannot obtain this token from school-account routes.\n\n**Host:** `x-school-host` is **not** checked (unlike POST). A valid token works even if the header is a school host.\n\n**Side effects:** none. Does not rotate or extend the token.\n\n**Success body:** `{ email, expiresAt }` — **no `token` field** (unlike sign-in).\n\n**Errors that exist:** `401 { \"error\": \"Unauthorized\" }` when the token is missing, empty, expired, or invalid. `405` for PUT/PATCH/etc.\n\n**Not used:** 400, 403, 404 (path exists), 409, 422."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('unauthenticated is 401 with error string', function () {",
                  "  if (pm.response.code !== 401) { return; }",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().error).to.eql('Unauthorized');",
                  "});",
                  "pm.test('success is 200 with email and expiresAt only', function () {",
                  "  if (pm.response.code !== 200) { return; }",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('email').that.is.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.have.property('expiresAt').that.is.a('string');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('token');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
