        {
          "name": "Sign out platform admin",
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                {
                  "key": "token",
                  "value": "{{accessToken}}",
                  "type": "string"
                }
              ]
            },
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}",
                "description": "The Next console sends this. The backend **ignores** it and does not revoke the HMAC token."
              },
              {
                "key": "x-school-host",
                "value": "{{adminHost}}",
                "description": "Sent by the Next console. **Not validated** on DELETE."
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/admin/session",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "admin",
                "session"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Client-side sign-out acknowledgement.\n\n**Auth:** not required. The handler does **not** call `readPlatformAdminSession`. Missing or invalid tokens still return 200.\n\n**Who:** the Next admin console calls this to drop its host-only cookie. Anyone who can reach the backend can call it; it is a no-op on the server.\n\n**Host:** not checked (unlike school-account DELETE, which can return 403 on the wrong host).\n\n**Side effects:** **none on the server.** HMAC tokens stay valid until `expiresAt`. The client must discard `{{accessToken}}` / the cookie. There is no deny-list.\n\n**Success:** always `200 { \"ok\": true }` for DELETE.\n\n**Errors that exist:** `405` for methods other than GET/POST/DELETE.\n\n**Not used:** 400, 401, 403, 404, 409, 422."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('sign-out is 200 { ok: true }', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200);",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.eql({ ok: true });",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
